        "Treat When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle as a control question: what would a reviewer need to repeat the check without asking? A rotation that works for a simple lead may fail when an account already has a relationship with a sender. Decide whether continuity or fairness takes priority in that case. Record the decision and share it with the team. Keep the note with the record so the next reviewer can compare the change.",
        "Treat When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle as a control question: what would a reviewer need to repeat the check without asking? A short case such as an existing customer with a new request is more useful than an abstract description. Review the examples when the rules change and update them together. The examples reduce the chance that two people interpret the same rule differently. Keep the note with the record so the next reviewer can compare the change."
