        "For When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle, start with the decision the record must support and the person who will review it. If records sit unacknowledged, the routing may be sending them to unavailable senders. If they are acknowledged but not worked, the issue is capacity or prioritization. Fix the actual cause rather than adding another notification. Test the revised rule on one live case and record what the team learned.",
        "The following cycle is a good moment to test When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle against one real case before changing the template. The list should be small enough to clear in a few minutes. If the same sender repeatedly leaves records unacknowledged, ask whether the routing or the workload is the cause before treating it as a performance issue. Ask a reviewer who did not prepare the item to restate the conclusion from the evidence."
