        "For When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle, start with the decision the record must support and the person who will review it. If the pilot meets them, expand gradually. If it does not, adjust the rules or abandon the model. Avoid a full switch based on a single good week. If the same question appears twice, fix the template rather than the answer.",
        "Before the next review, write down what When should a BDR team use a round-robin sender model in the next review cycle is meant to prevent and how the team would notice a gap. A rotation may improve response time while adding a step that the team dislikes. Record both so the final decision reflects the full cost. If the pilot requires manual work that will not scale, say so before expanding. If the same question appears twice, fix the template rather than the answer."
